Caliptra's testbench services start seven hexadecimal literals with an
underscore after the base, as in 512'h_8FA8... IEEE 1800-2023 5.7.1 says the
underscore "shall be legal anywhere in a number except as the first character",
and A.8.7 writes a hex_value as hex_digit { _ | hex_digit }, so its first
character is a digit. Drop the leading underscore; the value is the same.

The text is Caliptra's own, reported as
https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/issues/1438 and fixed there in
https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/pull/1439. Sent to the suite as
https://github.com/verilator/rtlmeter/pull/60

